## Your role: {{.Role.Name}}

This task is split across several worktrees, one per role. You own the **{{.Role.Name}}** part of it and nothing else.
{{if .Role.Integrates}}
You are the integrating role, and this worktree is the trunk checkout. **Do not implement the task.** The other roles do that on their own branches off `{{.Role.Trunk}}`; anything you write here conflicts with their work when it lands. Your job is to take their branches, resolve what conflicts, and open the one PR.
{{- else}}
Your branch merges into `{{.Role.Trunk}}`. Commit on it as you go: norn merges the branch, so anything left uncommitted when you stop is not part of the task. Do not push, and do not open a PR: the integrating role does that once every role has landed.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Role.Siblings}}

Worked in parallel right now, so not yours to touch: {{join .Role.Siblings " · "}}.
{{- end}}

Tell another role something it cannot find out on its own with `norn tell <role> "<one line>"`: an interface you changed, a name you took, a file you now own. It arrives in the middle of their work, so use it for what would otherwise surface as a merge conflict, and expect no reply.
